---
import ProductImage from "../components/ProductImage.astro";
import board from "../../../../docs/user/media/workbench/board.png";
import ticket from "../../../../docs/user/media/workbench/pull-requests.png";
import context from "../../../../docs/user/media/workbench/ticket-context.png";
import jira from "../../../../docs/user/media/workbench/jira-board.png";
import "../styles/site.css";

const repository = "https://github.com/filipgutica/t3code";
const guide = `${repository}/blob/main/docs/user/agent-workbench.md`;
const downloads = `${repository}/releases`;
const title = "T3 Code Workbench — A workspace for planning";
const description = "T3 Code, with a workspace for planning. Connect tickets, repository worktrees, native agent threads, and pull requests. Jira optional.";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const canonical = new URL(base, Astro.site);
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0b0c0e" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <link rel="icon" href={`${base}favicon.svg`} type="image/svg+xml" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={new URL(`${base}social.png`, Astro.site)} />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="T3 Code Workbench. A workspace for planning." />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-header wrap">
      <a class="brand" href={base} aria-label="T3 Code Workbench home">T3 Code <span>Workbench</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href={guide}>Guide</a>
        <a href={repository}>GitHub</a>
        <a class="button small" href={downloads}>Download Workbench</a>
      </nav>
    </header>
    <main id="main" class="wrap">
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <h1 id="hero-heading">T3 Code, with a workspace for planning.</h1>
          <p class="lead">Tickets, repositories, and agent conversations. Connected.</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="button" href={downloads}>Download Workbench</a>
            <a class="text-link" href={guide}>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
          <p class="provenance">An independent fork, regularly synced with upstream <a href="https://t3.codes">T3 Code</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="hero-media">
          <ProductImage src={board} alt="Orbit Workspace with tickets grouped by progress and scoped to API and web repositories" eager />
          <figcaption>One workspace for the work across your repositories.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="split section" aria-labelledby="scope-heading">
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2 id="scope-heading">One ticket. All the repositories it needs.</h2>
          <p>Group related repositories into a Workspace. Organize Tickets into Epics, describe the work, and choose the repositories it touches.</p>
          <p>When you create a Thread, Workbench prepares the Ticket’s Git worktrees. The description and repository paths are ready in the native T3 composer.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href={`${guide}#start-agent-work`}>See how a Ticket becomes a Thread <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <figure>
          <ProductImage src={ticket} alt="Workbench Ticket with its description, linked PRs, and prepared API and web worktrees" />
          <figcaption>Keep the intent and the repository scope together.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="section review-section" aria-labelledby="review-heading">
        <div class="review-heading">
          <h2 id="review-heading">From the plan to the pull requests.</h2>
          <p>Keep using native T3 Threads for agent work. Return to the Ticket to find its conversations, repository branches, and pull requests together.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="review-media">
          <figure>
            <h3>Start with the context attached.</h3>
            <ProductImage src={context} crop={{ x: 435, y: 245, width: 785, height: 740 }} alt="Native T3 composer with the Ticket description, acceptance criteria, and both repository paths" />
            <figcaption>Inspect the context, then send your first message.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <h3>Bring the results back to the Ticket.</h3>
            <ProductImage src={ticket} crop={{ x: 1015, y: 198, width: 385, height: 695 }} alt="Two linked pull requests from Orbit Web and Orbit API, above their prepared worktrees" />
            <figcaption>Follow pull requests across the repositories involved.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow" aria-label="Workbench workflow">
          <p><span>01</span><strong>Plan the work</strong>Tickets and Epics give the work a home.</p>
          <p><span>02</span><strong>Start a Thread</strong>Choose your agent and send the first message.</p>
          <p><span>03</span><strong>Review the result</strong>Follow the PRs, then mark the Ticket Done.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="split section jira-section" aria-labelledby="jira-heading">
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2 id="jira-heading">Your sprint, closer to the code.</h2>
          <p class="lead">Connect Jira, or keep your tickets local.</p>
          <p>Bring your assigned sprint issues into Workbench. Update descriptions and statuses, with repository scope and agent conversations attached to the work.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href={`${guide}#connect-jira`}>Explore the Jira workflow <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <figure>
          <ProductImage src={jira} alt="Orbit Jira Workspace with sprint issues and their workflow statuses" />
          <figcaption>Jira is optional. Local Tickets work on their own.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="closing section" aria-labelledby="closing-heading">
        <h2 id="closing-heading">Make room for the work around the code.</h2>
        <p>Workbench adds planning to the T3 Code experience.<br />Install Workbench alongside official T3 Code, with separate saved data.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href={downloads}>Download Workbench</a>
          <a class="text-link" href={guide}>Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <p class="release-note">Signed and notarized for macOS. See the release notes for platform downloads and update details.</p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer wrap">
      <a class="brand" href={base}>T3 Code <span>Workbench</span></a>
      <p>Built on <a href="https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code">T3 Code</a>. An independent, open-source fork.</p>
      <a href={repository}>Browse the source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
